"""
Chat Application (single-file edition)
Oasis Infobyte Internship - Python Programming (Advanced Tier)

Everything lives in one file: the socket/threading/SQLite server AND the
Tkinter GUI client. Pick which one to run with a command-line argument.

USAGE
-----
Run the server (do this first, in its own terminal):
    python chat_app.py server            # default port 12345
    python chat_app.py server 12345      # explicit port

Run a client (run this once per user, in its own terminal/window):
    python chat_app.py client
    python chat_app.py                   # "client" is the default mode

If you just want to try it out quickly on one machine with no separate
terminal for the server, run `python chat_app.py` and, when the client
can't reach a server, choose "Yes" on the prompt to auto-start a local
server in the background for you.

Server admin console commands (typed into the terminal running "server"):
    rooms                    -> list all rooms with online user counts
    users <room>             -> list users currently in <room>
    broadcast <message>      -> send a system message to every connected user
    kick <username>          -> forcibly disconnect a user
    help                     -> show available commands
    shutdown                 -> gracefully stop the server
"""

